    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok thanks. i want to make sure i'm being fair in my paper so i don't just dismiss them right away. could u expand on the specific scientific or statistical points they usually lean on to make their argument seem legitimate? like, what kind of data or studies do they typically point to when they try to defend the idea that these differences are biological rather than just social or environmental? i want to represent the \"strength\" of their position accurately.",
