      "content": "These arguments often draw upon historical analyses of cranial measurements or selective interpretations of heritability estimates from twin or adoption studies, which they extrapolate to group-level cognitive differences. Some proponents point to genetic studies that attempt to link specific genes to intelligence, suggesting that these genetic architectures differ among populations. They frequently overemphasize correlations found in certain cross-sectional data while downplaying the complexity of environmental influences or the limitations of those measurements.",
